				77,
				1
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Grove): Consolidate allow attributes in build script\n\nMove linter exception directives (`non_snake_case`, `dead_code`, `unused_*`) into `build.rs` as crate-level attributes at the file top. This aligns the build script configuration with the recent refactor in `Source/Library.rs` where similar directives were centralized to enforce strict PascalCase naming in core modules while permitting necessary exceptions for FFI and build artifacts.\n\nThis ensures `build.rs` remains compatible with the Rust compiler's build-time constraints without scattering allow directives, maintaining consistency with the updated `Cargo.toml` 2024 edition and the project's unified linter strategy.",
			"SHA": "64adbab7d0a8fe49705b1c24e5a7de36d38fa6bd"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-23T04:20:24Z",
			"File": [
				"⣿⠁⠀⠀⠀",
				77,
				18
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Grove): Consolidate linter rules and clean up dead code\n\nRemove redundant `#[allow(dead_code)]` and `#[allow(unused_*)]` attributes scattered across the Host, WASM, Transport, and API modules. These suppressions were masking legitimate unused fields and variables that will be utilized in upcoming implementation phases or are part of the VS Code API stubs.\n\nStandardize linter configuration by migrating all `#![allow(...)]` directives into `Source/Library.rs` (renamed from `lib.rs`). The new manifest enables `dead_code`, `unused_imports`, and `unexpected_cfgs` at the crate level to align with the FFI and WASM binding requirements, while retaining strict `missing_docs` and `clippy::all` warnings.\n\nUpdate `Cargo.toml` to use the 2024 edition, disable automatic binary/test generation, and correct the library entry point path to `Source/Library.rs`. Remove clippy-specific allow directives from `Source/main.rs` and `build.rs` to rely on the crate-level configuration.",
			"SHA": "3a54e0760073b0b95471b1144a53da1cabee7132"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-23T03:04:49Z",
			"File": [
				"⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				77,
				4
			],
			"Message": "fix(Grove): Re-enable non_snake_case allowance for main entry\n\nThe previous refactor inadvertently removed the `non_snake_case` allow attribute from `Source/main.rs`, which masked the FFI binding identifiers defined in `Source/Transport/gRPCTransport.rs` and `Source/Transport/IPCTransport.rs`. Since the `allow` directives in the transport files were also removed to enforce strict naming, the linter now flags valid FFI constant names in the main entry point.\n\nRestore the `non_snake_case` exception specifically in `Source/main.rs` while retaining the stricter `non_camel_case_types` and `non_upper_case_globals` exceptions in the transport modules where appropriate. This ensures FFI compatibility without relaxing the global PascalCase naming convention for core Rust identifiers.\n\nSimultaneously update the `Documentation/Rust` submodule to the latest upstream commit to align with current Rust documentation standards.",
			"SHA": "088c89170b6857e9d3af7414f68a511e975b5ae0"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-23T02:55:53Z",
			"File": [
				"⠇⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				77,
				6
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Grove): Remove redundant non_snake_case allow attribute\n\nThe `non_snake_case` allow attribute was propagated to the crate root and main entry point, inadvertently masking violations in Rust code that follows the project's strict PascalCase naming convention. This change removes the `non_snake_case` exception from `Source/lib.rs`, `Source/main.rs`, `Source/Transport/IPCTransport.rs`, and `Source/Transport/gRPCTransport.rs`, while retaining `non_camel_case_types` and `non_upper_case_globals` where required for FFI and C-style constants.\n\nSimultaneously, expand documentation in `Source/DevLog.rs` by adding inline comments to the `DedupState` struct and `NowNano` function to clarify their roles in log spam suppression and tracing.\n\nThis restores strict adherence to the CodeEditorLand PascalCase coding standards for all Rust identifiers.",
			"SHA": "fb826422e396b7d9464f6343ba3f2d78aaec7fb3"
		}
	],
